// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`rewrite.v5 prompt (F-16.14) > matches the golden messages: the Story notes in the system turn, the mood first in the user turn, no steer 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the rewrite feature inside a novel-writing app. Rewrite the passage the author selected so it reads as the author's own voice, as described below. Keep its meaning, its events, the names and facts it states, its point of view, its tense, and roughly its length. Remove generic or machine-sounding phrasing. Reply with the rewritten passage only, with the same paragraph breaks: no preamble, no notes, and no quotation marks around the answer. Match the author's voice:
- Narration is in past tense.

Story notes (the manuscript wins: where the passage and these notes disagree, follow the passage):
Here: Mara Vell (POV), Tomas Harrow
Named: The Hollow Elm, Wren
Mara Vell (from the book so far): Eyes: grey; Hair: cut short; Last seen at: the ferry landing.
Tomas Harrow (from the book so far): Role: ferryman.
Mara Vell (Mara, the Captain): Eyes: grey. Lost her brother Daven to the river at twelve; will not cross water at night.
Tomas Harrow (Tomas): Ferryman at the landing; owes the mill a debt he hides from Mara.
The Hollow Elm (the elm): A split elm on the north bank where the two met as children.
Tone (write in it): tense
Content (keep to it): grief
Themes (keep in view): debts come due

Scene: location Ferry landing, POV Mara Vell, timeline —.",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "Scene mood: quiet dread
Scene theme: debts come due
Keep the edit in line with them.

Text before:
"""
